  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 300 AM CDT Fri May 22 2026\n\nSaturday:\nAdditional shortwave energy builds into the region on Saturday,\nsupporting scattered shower and thunderstorm chances (40-70%).\nThe latest trends suggest a system building out of northeast OK\ninto southwest MO through the afternoon, and gradually moving\nthrough the area Saturday evening/night. There is a low end\npotential for some localized heavy rainfall and flooding given\nthe saturated soils from previous heavy rainfall this week.\nSaturday will also feature the return of near average\ntemperatures with subtle mid-level height rises into the region.\nHighs on Saturday return to the upper 70s and lower 80s.\n\nSunday-Thursday:\nAn active pattern persists into Sunday and beyond into next week\nwith ensemble guidance highlighting a series of shortwaves\nprogged to translate through the central CONUS. Guidance vary on\nexact timing and location of each wave, and thus the extent of\nrain chances and coverage. Nonetheless, additional rain chances\nremain in the forecast through much of next week, including\nMemorial Day on Monday. It worth noting, Sunday and Monday\nfeature lower rain chances (20-50%). With that being said, there\nwill be periods of dry time and all day washouts are currently\nnot expected. The highest rain chances (50-80%) are centered on\nTuesday of next week. The environment remains marginal at best,\nwith severe weather not expected to be in play at this time.",
